'   the failure it exists to avoid . _spec/internal/sbx/virtiofs-cwd-invalidation.puml
'   the mount plan it overrides .... _spec/internal/workspace/mount-model.puml
'   the trees it keeps out ........ _spec/packages/lib/dependency-trees.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHY CLONE IS THE DEFAULT ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' On, unless PROVEO_CLONE turns it off — and an explicit `--clone=false` still
' wins over the environment, flag over env being the rule everywhere else.
'
' It is the only shape in which the checkout is never written, no host-built
' dependency tree crosses into the sandbox, and — the reason it BECAME the
' default — the workspace lives on the VM's own disk instead of the virtiofs
' passthrough, whose directory entries have been measured vanishing under a
' running agent and taking every Bash call with them.
'
' sbx can only clone what git can: the MAIN worktree of a repository, offered
' as the primary workspace. Where the default cannot apply, the run falls back
' to the mounted checkout and SAYS WHY. An explicit --clone in those shapes is
' an error rather than a fallback, because it asked for a promise that cannot
' be kept.
'
' ── A LINKED WORKTREE CLONES THROUGH ITS MAIN WORKTREE ─────────────────────
' A linked worktree's .git is a FILE, so sbx cannot clone it. Until 2026-09-29
' that made it fall back to the mounted checkout, and the mount carried two
' hazards at once: the worktree over virtiofs, and — to reach the shared .git —
' the MAIN worktree mounted read-write beside it. Measured on
' proveo-claudecode-1b3fcb7f (2026-09-24 → 09-28): a Linux `pnpm install` in
' the sandbox rewrote ~/Projects/pluvo/worktrees/dev/node_modules with
' @nx/nx-linux-arm64-* only, and nx on the Mac then died with
' "WorkspaceContext is not a constructor".
'
' sbx itself refuses the direct route: `sbx create --clone` from a linked
' worktree fails with "--clone is not supported when run from a Git worktree
' … run from the main repository instead" (probed 2026-09-29). So the clone is
' of the MAIN worktree, at the main worktree's path — and every branch lives in
' the shared refs, so it carries the worktree's branch as origin/<branch>.
'
' The FIRST cut checked that branch out in the clone itself, and the agent then
' started in ~/Projects/pluvo/monorepo although the operator launched in
' ~/Projects/pluvo/worktrees/dev: the wrong prompt path, and /resume found none
' of the sessions Claude Code keys by that cwd. So the layout inside the VM is
'   <main path>      the sbx clone, left on its own branch
'   <worktree path>  `git worktree add` of that clone, on the worktree's branch
' — a real linked worktree at the host worktree's own path, on the VM's disk,
' sharing the clone's .git. The agent, PROVEO_WORKDIR, the .env link, the
' installs, and the teardown snapshot and lift all use the worktree path; the
' refs/heads/* fetch sees its commits because the .git is shared.
'
' Four mechanics make that path reachable:
'   sbx makes the parents of mount points root-owned, and the agent is uid 1000
'     with no sudo, so a ROOT kit startup command (WorktreeDirCommand) creates
'     the worktree directory owned by 1000; the seed then waits up to 10s for it
'     to be writable, since startup order is not documented;
'   paths are passed RESOLVED (realPath): sbx mounts /private/var/…, and an
'     unresolved /var/… names the VM's own /var — measured in the e2e;
'   sbx starts the agent in the primary workspace, so proveo-await-seed (the
'     claude/opencode/hermes shims exec it; bash.bashrc cds to its --cwd) moves
'     a launch from PROVEO_CLONE_MAIN into PROVEO_WORKDIR — only from exactly
'     there, so a claude started by hand elsewhere stays put, and only when the
'     worktree exists, so a failed add leaves the agent in the clone;
'   an existing worktree is left alone, so a reattached boot never moves an
'     agent off a branch it chose.
' The sandbox is NAMED for the worktree, not the main worktree it clones, or a
' worktree run would reattach to the main checkout's VM. A detached HEAD clones
' only when some branch holds it — sbx clones branches, so an orphan commit
' would never reach the clone.
' Uncommitted edits in the worktree stay on the host, as they do for the main
' checkout, and the run says so.
'
' ── THE PROJECT .env IS STAGED, NOT CLONED ─────────────────────────────────
' .env is gitignored, so a clone never carries it, and until 2026-09-29 the
' agent simply ran without one — the mounted checkout it replaced always had
' it. The operator first chose a READ-ONLY mount; on 2026-10-07 the operator
' asked that sandbox edits reach the host, and chose a TEARDOWN WRITE-BACK over
' a live rw mount of the real file. A live mount of the real file would hand
' the agent every provider key the broker strips; the write-back never does.
' sbx mounts directories only, and the directory holding the real .env is the
' repository root — the clone target itself. So stageCloneEnv copies the
' project's .env (ProjectEnvFile: the input dir's, else the repo root's; a
' worktree's symlink resolves to the main checkout's) into
' <state>/sbx/project-env/.env (0600), which is mounted read-only, and
' proveo_clone_env symlinks $PROVEO_WORKDIR/.env to it before the release.
' It is a per-run snapshot: host edits land on the next run.
' Under --credentials broker the copy DROPS every provider key variable, since
' sbx's proxy attaches those and the agent must never hold them; forward keeps
' the file whole. /.env goes into the clone's .git/info/exclude, so a project
' that forgot to ignore it still never commits the link at teardown, and an
' existing .env in a reattached clone is left alone and reported.
'
' ── .env EDITS MERGE HOME BY NAME AT TEARDOWN ──────────────────────────────
' The staged dir is mounted READ-WRITE, and stageCloneEnv keeps the staged
' bytes as <state>/sbx/project-env.base, OUTSIDE the mount, so the agent
' cannot move the baseline. At teardown writeBackCloneEnv reads the clone's
' .env over `sbx exec cat` — an editor that saves by rename replaces the
' symlink, and the staged file then never sees the edit — and falls back to
' the staged file when the sandbox is gone. MergeProjectEnv applies base →
' edited onto the host file NAME BY NAME:
'   a name the host also changed during the run keeps the HOST value (warned;
'     the clone's version stays in the staged file);
'   a brokered key is REFUSED: the sandbox never writes one, and the host's
'     own line, absent from base, survives untouched;
'   comments, order and every untouched line stay byte for byte.
' The host file is replaced atomically and keeps its mode. ProjectEnvFile
' resolves symlinks at staging, so a worktree whose .env links the monorepo's
' stages AND writes back the monorepo's own file: the rename swaps the target,
' every worktree link keeps pointing at it, and the edit cascades to all.
' Only the run's own teardown (TeardownClone) writes back. retireSandbox runs
' PreserveClone with the NEXT run's fresh baseline, against which the old
' clone's .env would read as edits and revert host changes.
'
' ── A TRACKED _spec IS LIFTED INTO THE HOST WORKTREE ───────────────────────
' A symlinked _spec is relinked to its mounted target, so edits are live. A
' TRACKED _spec rode the clone, so its edits reached the host only as commits
' under refs/proveo/<sid>/ — never in the operator's working tree. On
' 2026-10-07 the operator chose a teardown lift over a live side-mount: a
' symlink over a tracked dir is a typechange the snapshot commit would record.
' The seed records the clone's starting HEAD once, at the git-path
' proveo-clone-base (per worktree, on the VM's disk so a reboot cannot reset
' it), only when PROVEO_CLONE_WORKSPACE says the tree is a clone — never into
' a mounted checkout's .git. After the refs arrive, liftClonedSpec diffs
' base..HEAD under _spec and `git restore --worktree`s each changed path from
' the clone's HEAD, SKIPPING any path the host changed since base (tracked or
' untracked). The index is never touched. The base then moves to HEAD, so the
' next run lifts only its own work.
'
' ── POST-EXIT LISTS BRANCHES GIT RECORDED AS PUSHED ────────────────────────
' A successful push writes "update by push" on the remote-tracking reflog.
' That log lives in the common git dir, so one `git log -g --all` from any
' worktree includes pushes made in every linked worktree. proveo keeps the
' lines whose reflog time is at or after the run started, and prints each
' branch once (`pushed origin/name`). A clone is queried inside the sandbox
' before it is removed. A direct checkout is queried on the host.
'
' ── THE SEED ASSERTS THE SHARES BEFORE IT RELEASES THE AGENT ───────────────
' PROVEO_SHARES lists rel=rw|ro for each of _spec and .env the HOST holds at
' the agent workdir: a clone is always rw; a mounted checkout follows its
' bind. proveo_assert_shares runs after the clone steps and before the
' instructions; a path that is missing, unreadable, or read-only where rw was
' promised writes /dev/shm/proveo-seed-refused and returns 1, so the release
' marker is never written. sbx's startup wrapper still exits 0 (a seed miss
' must not tear the sandbox down), so the GATE is proveo-await-seed: it stops
' waiting when the refusal appears, and refuses an agent launch with the
' reason; `--cwd` still answers so a shell can inspect. A file whose only line
' is "OpenCode credential preflight refused release" is the runtime's own note
' from a kept sandbox; await-seed deletes it and launches. Docker never sets
' PROVEO_SHARES, and a host without _spec or .env asserts nothing.
'
' ── IGNORED HOST SYMLINKS ARE RELINKED, NOT CLONED ─────────────────────────
' The same gap took _spec: ~/Projects/pluvo/<worktree>/_spec is a symlink to
' ~/Syncd/pluvo/_spec and .gitignore:152 ignores it, so the clone had no _spec
' while its TARGET was mounted — an agent in worktrees/main reported "No _spec/
' tree exists in this worktree" (2026-09-29). The mount plan already resolves
' every escaping symlink (workspace.Link, LinkMounted); cloneLinks hands the
' mounted ones to the seed as PROVEO_CLONE_LINKS (rel=target, '|'-separated)
' and proveo_clone_links recreates each one the clone lacks, before the
' release, excluded in .git/info/exclude. A path the clone already has is never
' replaced, a rel with ".." is refused, and .env stays with its own policy
' (LinkEnvPolicy) rather than riding this list.
'
' ── THE REGRESSION GUARD DRIVES THE REAL RUN ───────────────────────────────
' TestCloneLeavesTheHostTreeAlone launches `proveo run claudecode --clone
' --shell` rather than the `sbx create --clone` it used to build by hand. What
' it guards — the decideClone verdict, the dropped nested bind, the lift at
' teardown — is then proveo's own assembly rather than a replica, and a replica
' agrees with itself indefinitely while the run it stands in for moves.
' TestCloneModeLandsTheCloneAndLiftsTheOutputDir already worked this way, so the
' two now share one launch shape (_spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml).
' TestCloneCarriesAGitignoredSymlinkedDotEnv uses the same shape for the staged
' .env: gitignored, symlinked out of the checkout, it must read back in the
' clone, accept a write, stay out of `git status`, and land that write in the
' host target at teardown. It asserts on .env alone, because the instructions
' seed leaves AGENTS.md untracked in the clone. TestCloneLiftsTrackedSpecEdits
' edits a tracked _spec in the clone and reads the edit back from the host
' worktree after teardown.
'
' ── NOTHING MAY BE MOUNTED UNDER THE REPOSITORY IN CLONE MODE ──────────────
' sbx clones only into an EMPTY workspace, and it mounts every positional
' workspace at its own host path. So an output dir nested under the repository
' (<repo>/reports) was mounted INTO the clone target before the clone ran, the
' target was no longer empty, and sbx skipped the clone WITHOUT A WORD. The
' agent then sat in a root-owned directory holding nothing but `reports/`, with
' the real checkout read-only at /run/sandbox/source — measured 2026-09-02 on
' proveo-1788366117-41470 and reproduced with a throwaway repo.
'
' The nested bind is therefore dropped in clone mode. The output dir is lifted
' back at teardown; anything else nested is simply not mounted, and both are
' said out loud.
'
' ── HOW THE WORK GETS BACK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A snapshot commit first, of whatever the agent left UNCOMMITTED, so the fetch
' that follows carries it — only when there is something to commit, since a
' clean tree earns no empty commit, and under an author that says who made it.
' `sbx rm` drops the clone with the VM and sbx's own guidance is to fetch or
' push before removing; an agent that stopped mid-edit has nothing to push.
'
' Then every branch is fetched into refs/proveo/<sid>/. REFS, not a
' remote-tracking namespace: sbx removes its sandbox-<name> remote with the
' sandbox, and `git remote remove` deletes refs/remotes/<remote>/* with it.
' refs/proveo/ is proveo's own and outlives both.
'
' ── THE SANDBOX IS REUSED; THE REF NAMESPACE IS NOT ────────────────────────
' These two keys look like one and are not. The SANDBOX is named for the def
' and its workspace (`proveo-<target>-<workspace fingerprint>`) so a second run
' re-attaches to the VM the first one built — `sbx run --name` reads the
' workspace out of the existing sandbox's spec, which is why the workspace is
' in the key: a different project under the same def must not inherit the
' first one's mounts.
'
' The REFS stay keyed to the SESSION, because the fetch is a force fetch
' (`+refs/heads/*`). A namespace as stable as the sandbox would have each run
' overwrite the work the last one left on the host — the one thing this whole
' path exists to preserve. CloneFetchArgs therefore takes both: the sandbox
' names the remote, the session names the destination.
'
' ── EITHER DELIVERY ROUTE IS ARRIVAL, AND A TEST MUST ACCEPT BOTH ──────────
' The two renderings put the agent's commit in different places, so a probe
' asking "did the work reach the host" has to look in both. The DOCKER rendering
' advances the mounted worktree's own HEAD as the agent commits; the SANDBOX
' rendering commits inside a clone and lands nothing until teardown fetches it
' into refs/proveo/<sid>/. `hostCarriesCommit` in e2e/git_access_test.go
' therefore waits for the session to exit and then reads `git log --all
' --glob=refs/proveo/*`. A `git log -1` on HEAD is a docker fact wearing a git
' claim, and pinning the backend to make it true again is banned
' (_spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml).
'
' ── THE ONE LEG THAT COULD NOT WORK WHEN IT WAS NEEDED ─────────────────────
' The `sandbox-<name>` git remote is served by a DAEMON that lives only while
' the sandbox RUNS. And the case this whole mechanism exists for is an agent
' that CRASHED — which leaves the sandbox STOPPED. So the single transport home
' depended on precisely the condition the failure takes away.
'
' Measured on run proveo-1788799575-162088 (2026-09-07). Same sandbox, same
' moment, three copy-outs:
'
'   snapshot commit over `sbx exec`   SUCCEEDED
'   output-dir tar over `sbx exec`    SUCCEEDED
'   ref fetch over the git remote     refused, errno=Connection refused
'                                     on 127.0.0.1
'
' Nothing else about the sandbox had gone away. The difference is only that
' `sbx exec` does not need the daemon to be listening, and the remote does.
'
' Two more things pointed the wrong way. `PreserveClone` guarded on sbx.Exists
' and not sbx.Running, so it ALWAYS attempted the doomed fetch. And the fallback
' it printed — "if the sandbox still exists, `git fetch sandbox-<name>` by hand"
' — failed identically, while the very next line offered `sbx rm --force`, which
' DESTROYS the work the operator had just been sent to rescue.
'
' ── THE FIX: RUNNING NEGOTIATES, STOPPED STREAMS ───────────────────────────
' Two transports, chosen by state and not by hope. A RUNNING sandbox still
' negotiates over its git remote: that is cheap and incremental, and git works
' out what the host is missing. A STOPPED one — or a running one whose remote
' refuses, which is tried first and reported as a NOTE before falling through —
' streams `git bundle create --quiet - --branches` out over `sbx exec`, and the
' host fetches that bundle into the SAME refs/proveo/<name>/*. A bundle is a
' valid git remote, so the destination refspec is identical and the work lands
' in the same place whichever leg carried it.
'
' The bundle is BOUNDED by an exclusion list, or it would carry the whole
' history. The list is the host's own branch tips (CloneHostTipsArgs, capped at
' CloneHostTipsCap = 64), filtered IN THE CONTAINER with `git cat-file -e` down
' to the ones the clone actually has. An id the clone does not know is skipped
' silently, which is exactly what makes an over-broad list SAFE: more exclusions
' only make the bundle smaller, so a repository with thousands of branches is an
' argv-length problem and never a correctness one. What ships is the agent's new
' commits, not the repository.
'
' Exit 4 (CloneBundleEmpty) means "the clone holds no commit the host lacks".
' That is a NOTE and not a failure: nothing went wrong and there is nothing to
' carry, and reporting it as an error teaches the operator to ignore the one
' line that matters on the day something does go wrong.
'
' The tip list is interpolated into a shell script, so a candidate that is not a
' plain object name is DROPPED rather than quoted — a ref name can hold almost
' any byte, and none of them belong in an argv proveo builds by hand. And
' `for c in ; do` is a syntax error, so the loop is emitted only when there is
' something to loop over; no tips means no exclusions, which is a correct bundle
' and merely a larger one.
'
' The rescue recipe printed on total failure uses exec+bundle too. Printing the
' daemon recipe there was printing the leg that had just been measured refusing
' connections.
'
' The output dir is copied out separately, as a tar stream on stdout. Untracked
' and usually gitignored, deliverables are exactly what the ref fetch leaves
' behind. The archive's members are relative to the clone root, so unpacking
' under the host repo root recreates the same path, and tar refuses absolute
' members and `..` on its own. Failure is a WARNING naming the sandbox, so the
' operator can still `sbx exec` the files out before removing it.
'
' Both copy-outs pass `-w /`: the container WorkingDir can stop resolving
' mid-run, and an exec that inherits it dies at chdir before a byte moves.
title sbx clone mode — a private workspace, and the two paths home

actor "operator" as OP

node "host repository" as REPO <<host>> {
  database "the checkout\nNEVER written in clone mode" as SRC <<db>>
  database "refs/proveo/<sid>/*\nproveo's own namespace, outlives the remote" as REFS <<db>>
  database "<repo>/reports\nthe output dir, unpacked from a tar stream" as OUT <<db>>
}

node "sbx sandbox" as BOX <<app>> {
  component "git clone\ninto an EMPTY workspace, on the VM's own disk" as CLONE <<app>>
  component "the agent" as AGENT <<app>>
  component "snapshot commit\nonly when the tree is dirty" as SNAP <<app>>
  component "git bundle --branches\nstreamed out over ""sbx exec""" as BUNDLE <<app>>
}

component "the sandbox-<name> git daemon\nlistening only while the sandbox RUNS" as GITD <<error>>

component "virtiofs passthrough\ndirectory entry vanishes under a running agent" as VFS <<error>>
component "a nested bind under the repo\nleaves the clone target non-empty" as NESTED <<error>>
component "host-built dependency trees\ncannot execute in the container" as TREES <<error>>

OP ARROW_MAIN CLONE : ""--clone"", the default since 2026-09-01
SRC ARROW_MAIN CLONE : read once
CLONE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : a workspace on the VM's disk
AGENT ARROW_MAIN SNAP : at teardown, if dirty
SNAP ARROW_MAIN GITD : RUNNING: negotiate over the remote
GITD ARROW_MAIN REFS : ""+refs/heads/*:refs/proveo/<sid>/*""
SNAP ARROW_MAIN BUNDLE : STOPPED, or the remote refused
BUNDLE ARROW_MAIN REFS : the SAME refspec, from a bundle file
AGENT ARROW_QUEUE OUT : tar on stdout, unpacked host-side
CLONE ARROW_ERROR VFS : what clone avoids
CLONE ARROW_ERROR TREES : what clone keeps out
NESTED ARROW_ERROR CLONE : silently skips the clone

note bottom of CLONE
  **Only what git can clone.** The MAIN worktree
  of a repository, as the primary workspace.
  Elsewhere the run falls back to the mounted
  checkout and says why; an explicit ""--clone""
  there is an error, not a fallback.
end note

note as WORKTREE
  **A linked worktree clones its main worktree.**
  The seed adds a VM-local worktree at the host
  worktree's path, and the agent starts there. The
  old mount rewrote the host's node_modules.
end note

note as CLONEGUARD
  **The guard launches the product it guards.**
  A hand-built ""sbx create --clone"" agrees with
  itself indefinitely, so the regression case
  now exercises ""proveo run --clone --shell""
  and reads the decideClone verdict it recorded.
end note

note bottom of NESTED
  **It failed SILENTLY, which is why the bind is
  dropped.** sbx clones only into an empty dir,
  so a nested mount arriving first left the agent
  in a root-owned directory holding nothing but
  ""reports/"" and no clone.
end note

note bottom of SNAP
  **A clean tree earns no empty commit.** ""sbx rm""
  drops the clone with the VM, and an agent that
  stopped mid-edit has nothing to push — so the
  snapshot is what makes the fetch carry the work.
end note

note bottom of GITD
  **It dies with the crash it exists for.**
  Measured on proveo-1788799575-162088, 2026-09-07:
  ""errno=Connection refused"" on 127.0.0.1, while
  the snapshot commit and the output tar succeeded
  over ""sbx exec"" on that same stopped sandbox.
end note

note bottom of BUNDLE
  **Bounded, so it carries the work and not the
  history.** The host's branch tips (capped at 64)
  are filtered IN THE CONTAINER by ""git cat-file
  -e"", so an over-broad list is safe. Exit 4 means
  "nothing the host lacks" — a note, not a failure.
end note

note as DELIVERY
  **Either route counts as arrival.** Docker moves
  the mounted worktree's own HEAD; the sandbox
  lands the work under ""refs/proveo/<sid>/"" at
  teardown, so a probe reading ""log -1"" alone
  asserts a docker fact dressed as a git one.
end note

note bottom of REFS
  **Refs, not remote-tracking.** ""git remote
  remove"" deletes ""refs/remotes/<remote>/*"" with
  the remote sbx tears down. ""refs/proveo/"" is
  proveo's own and survives it.
end note

note as SHARES
  **No release without the shares.** The seed
  asserts _spec and .env at the workdir; a miss
  writes the refusal, and proveo-await-seed
  will not launch the agent past it.
end note

note as ENVBACK
  **.env merges home by name.** A host-side
  change wins, a brokered key is refused, and
  every untouched line stays byte for byte.
end note

note bottom of OUT
  **Lifted, because it could not be mounted.**
  Deliverables are untracked and gitignored, so
  the ref fetch leaves them behind. A failure
  warns and names the sandbox, so the operator
  can still ""sbx exec"" them out.
end note

note bottom of VFS
  **The reason clone became the default.** A
  directory entry measured vanishing inside the
  VM while the host directory stayed put; every
  Bash call then exits 1 with no output.
end note
@enduml
